## Alternatives considered

- **In-place incremental polish without a manifest**: leaves duplicated facts and unowned legacy files across sessions and risks deleting buried rationale before extraction.

## Acceptance criteria

- All `EXTRACT_NOTE` / `EXTRACT_RECORD` rows (and any falsified-theory extractions) land before any `ARCHIVE` / `DELETE` row or `docs/theory.md` rewrite executes.
- Rebuilt current-state docs (and `docs/theory.md`, if enabled) pass `doc-verify` against authoritative code, tests, proofs/studies, or named owners.
- Deterministic gate exits `0` with zero broken inline relative Markdown links checked by the baseline gate and zero tracked `.agents/scratch/` files (run `lychee` or a dedicated link check separately when angle-bracket links or external/published URLs matter).

## Risks

- Deleting legacy docs before verifying external links or buried rationale; mitigated by clean-tree preflight, extract-first batching, and explicit user grill on ambiguous files.
